-<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">SC Down Payment Help</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Buying a home</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Down payment help in Horry County:<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">you do not have to be a <span style="white-space:nowrap">first-time buyer.</span></em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 1, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">SC Housing gives an eligible buyer $10,000. Most houses for sale in Conway, Loris, Aynor and Longs are under its price limit. Across the beach towns, about a third are.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The $10,000 is a second mortgage from SC Housing, the state's housing agency, and it pays toward the down payment and closing costs. SC Housing forgives it after you have lived in the home 15 years. If you sell, refinance or move out sooner, you repay all of it, from the sale or the new loan.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">To qualify, a household of one or two can earn up to $114,960, or $134,120 for three or more. The home can cost up to $450,000, you need a credit score of 640, and you must own no other property when the loan closes.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Homes that fit SC Housing's limits, sent to you</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Get the list</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#qualify" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Do you qualify</a></li><li><a href="#paying-it-back" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Paying it back</a></li><li><a href="#which-homes" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which homes</a></li><li><a href="#no-money-down" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">No money down</a></li><li><a href="#which-program" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which program</a></li><li><a href="#local-help" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Local help</a></li><li><a href="#how-to-apply" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">How to apply</a></li><li><a href="#sc-housing-questions" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;c