 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a retired couple have to file a South Carolina tax return?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A married couple, both 65 or older, does not have to file a South Carolina return unless their South Carolina income is over $60,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I apply for the homestead exemption in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Apply at the Horry County Auditor's office, and inside a city at the city too, by July 15 for that year's bill. You must own the home and live in it as your legal home. The exemption takes the first $50,000 of the home's value off the tax."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I lose the 4 percent rate if I rent the home out?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only if you rent it out for more than 72 days in a calendar year. State law keeps the 4 percent rate on a home you live in as long as it is not rented for more than 72 days in that year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What makes a community 55+ under federal law?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"To count as 55+ housing under federal fair housing law, a community needs at least one person 55 or older in at least 80 percent of its occupied homes. It must also publish and follow its age policy, and check ages."}}]}</script>
