-bottom:1rem">The answer depends on the kind of home you want.</p><ul class="c3-va-pick" role="list" aria-label="Can you use a VA loan on the home you want"><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span class="k">A house you will live in</span><span class="v"><span class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)">Can you use VA: </span><i class="yes">Yes</i></span><span class="d">No list to check. The seller and the VA appraisal decide.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5l5-3V21M10 21V4h9v17M13 8h3M13 12h3M13 16h3M7.5 13h.01M7.5 16.5h.01"/></svg></span><span class="k">A townhouse</span><span class="v"><span class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)">Can you use VA: </span><i class="yes">Yes</i></span><span class="d">If the community was set up as a condo, it must also be on the VA's condo list.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8.5 18.5V3.5l8 3.6-8 3.6M3.5 19c0-1.4 3.8-2.5 8.5-2.5s8.5 1.1 8.5 2.5-3.8 2.5-8.5 2.5-8.5-1.1-8.5-2.5z"/><circle cx="16" cy="15.2" r="1.2"/></svg></span><span class="k">A condo in a villa, golf or townhome community</span><span class="v"><span class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)">Can you use VA: </span><i class="maybe">If listed</i></span><span class="d">Only in a community on the VA's list. <a href="#va-approved-condos" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The listed communities with condos for sale</a> are named below.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span><span class="k">A condo in an oceanfront resort tower</span><span class="v"><span class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)">Can you use VA: </span><i class="no">Rarely</i></span><span class="d">Only 2 of the 29 big oceanfront resort buildings we track are on the VA's list.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span class="k">A beach second home or a rental</span><span class="v"><span class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)">Can you use VA: </span><i class="no">No</i></span><span class="d">A VA loan is only for the home you live in.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 20.5v-1a5 5 0 0 1 5-5h2a5 5 0 0 1 5 5v1M16 14.5h1a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v2"/><circle cx="8.5" cy="7" r="3.2"/><circle cx="17" cy="8.8" r="2.5"/></svg></span><span class="k">A house with 2 to 4 units</span><span class="v"><span class="sr-only" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)">Can you use VA: </span><i class="yes">Yes</i></span><span class="d">You must live in one of the units. You can rent the others.</span></li></ul><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes for sale marked as taking a VA loan, out of every 100"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes for sale marked as taking a VA loan, out of every 100</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Kind of home</span><span role="columnheader">marked VA</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Houses</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.52" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">52 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Townhouses</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.46" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">46 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">All condos</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.09" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">9 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Condos with a rental program</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.04" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">4 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Condos in an oceanfront building</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.03" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">3 in 100</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Chapter3's count of homes for sale on the Coastal Carolinas MLS, in aggregate, from the financing the listing says the seller will consider. A condo in a building with a rental program, or in an oceanfront building, is also counted in all condos.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="va-approved-condos"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="VA-approved condos">Which condos in Myrtle Beach are VA-approved?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The <a href="https://lgy.va.gov/lgyhub/condo-report" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA's condo list</a> holds about 175 condo communities in Horry County, many more than HUD's list for FHA loans.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">These communities on the list had condos for sale on the day we counted, from Carolina Forest to Longs:</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:49.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Condo communities on the VA's list with condos for sale now</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Community</th><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col" class="n">Condos for sale</th><th scope="col">Asking prices</th><th scope="col">Bedrooms</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Windsor Green</th><td data-label="Where">Carolina Forest</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">12</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$170,000 to $200,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Magnolia Pointe</th><td data-label="Where">Myrtle Beach, inland</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">36</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$210,000 to $350,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">2 to 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Magnolia North</th><td data-label="Where">Myrtle Beach, inland</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">30</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$140,000 to $340,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">1 to 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">The Village at Queens Harbour</th><td data-label="Where">Myrtle Beach, inland</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">14</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$150,000 to $280,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">1 to 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Shorewood</th><td data-label="Where">Myrtle Beach, inland</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">11</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$140,000 to $220,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">2 to 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Seagate Village</th><td data-label="Where">Myrtle Beach</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">5</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$250,000 to $300,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Monterey Bay Suites</th><td data-label="Where">Myrtle Beach, oceanfront</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">30</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$100,000 to $210,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">1</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Southbridge</th><td data-label="Where">Surfside Beach</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">10</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$150,000 to $230,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">1 to 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Park West</th><td data-label="Where">Murrells Inlet</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">6</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$220,000 to $330,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">2 to 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Myrtle Greens</th><td data-label="Where">Conway</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">7</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$110,000 to $160,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">1 to 2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">The Havens at Barefoot</th><td data-label="Where">North Myrtle Beach</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">12</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$230,000 to $480,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">2 to 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Edgewater</th><td data-label="Where">North Myrtle Beach</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">10</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$250,000 to $570,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">2 to 4</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Carolina Keyes</th><td data-label="Where">North Myrtle Beach</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">10</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$170,000 to $400,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">1 to 2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Carolina Yacht Landing</th><td data-label="Where">Little River</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">23</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$170,000 to $330,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">2 to 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tullamore Lakes</th><td data-label="Where">Longs</td><td class="n" data-label="Condos for sale">4</td><td data-label="Asking prices">$140,000 to $190,000</td><td data-label="Bedrooms">2 to 3</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the oceanfront the list is short. Monterey Bay Suites, in the table, has one-bedroom suites for sale. Of the big resort buildings, Beach Cove Resort and the Renaissance Tower at Myrtle Beach Resort are on the list. Our <a href="/invest/condo-buildings/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">condo building directory</a> covers the rest of the oceanfront.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How does a community get on the VA's list?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Your lender can ask the VA to review it, with the condo's papers. Over the past year, most of the VA's reviews of condo communities here ended with the community on the list. Our guide to <a href="/invest/non-warrantable-condos/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">condos most lenders will not lend on</a> covers the other loan rules a condo building can fail.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Is your building on the VA's list?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the building's name, or the area and price you want. We look it up on the VA's list and send you the condos for sale in listed communities.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask about a building</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="sellers"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Sellers who take VA">Do sellers in Myrtle Beach accept VA offers?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most do inland, fewer at the beach.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Houses for sale marked as taking a VA loan, by town"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Houses for sale marked as taking a VA loan, by town</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Town</span><span role="columnheader">share marked VA</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Conway</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.67" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">67%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Longs</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.67" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">67%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Aynor</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.61" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">61%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Loris</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.6" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">60%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Little River</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.56" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">56%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.5" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">50%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Murrells Inlet</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.41" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">41%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Surfside Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.37" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">37%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.28" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">28%</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Towns are mailing addresses, so Myrtle Beach includes Carolina Forest and Socastee, and Conway includes country land outside the city.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inland towns give a VA buyer the most choice. Conway also has the highest city tax, so a fully exempt veteran saves the most there. Our guides to <a href="/submarkets/conway/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Conway</a> and <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Carolina Forest</a> show what living there is like.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">VA is most common in the middle of the market, and about 7 in 10 new houses for sale are marked VA. Our <a href="/buyers/new-construction/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">new construction guide</a> covers buying from a builder.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A listing without the VA mark can still take a VA offer. On a house you like that is not marked, we ask the listing agent whether the seller will take VA before you make an offer.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Flood zones</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 3 in 10 houses for sale listed as in a flood zone are marked VA. In a high-risk flood zone, a VA loan requires flood insurance for the life of the loan. Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance guide</a> gives what it costs.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Taking over a seller's VA loan</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A buyer can take over a seller's VA loan instead of getting a new one. This is called assuming the loan. Only 18 homes for sale on the Grand Strand are listed with a loan you can take over, of any kind, so we ask the seller's agent about the loan on each home you like.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Houses for sale that take VA</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the towns you like and your price range. We send you the houses for sale there that are marked as taking a VA loan, and we show you the ones you pick.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Get the list</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="second-homes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Second homes and rentals">Can you buy a beach house or a rental with a VA loan?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Only as the home you live in. You can buy a house with 2 to 4 units, live in one and rent the others, but few sellers of these homes here mark VA: 3 of the 61 for sale.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A beach second home or a pure rental does not qualify. You certify that you intend to move in. If you are on active duty and cannot live there because of it, your spouse can meet the rule.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="property-tax"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Property tax exemption">Do disabled veterans pay property tax in South Carolina?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not on their home, if the VA rates them permanently and totally disabled from their service. The exemption covers the home they own and live in, alone or with a spouse, with up to 5 acres, and up to two cars. A lower rating does not qualify.</p><figure style="margin:1.2rem 0 1rem;max-width:620px"><table class="c3-va-tbl"><caption>Tax a fully exempt veteran saves each year, on a home the county values at $400,000</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Where the home is</th><th scope="col">Tax saved a year</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Conway</th><td>$2,610</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">North Myrtle Beach</th><td>$1,790</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Surfside Beach</th><td>$1,680</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">City of Myrtle Beach</th><td>$1,620</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Murrells Inlet or Garden City<small>Horry County side</small></th><td>$1,570</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Outside the cities<small>Carolina Forest, Socastee, Little River</small></th><td>$1,470</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.55;margin-top:.6rem">Chapter3's figures from the county's tax rates for a home you live in, worked out the same way as our property tax calculator. The county taxes its own value of the home, not the price you paid. Small special district taxes and the county's stormwater fee are left out.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A surviving spouse who has not remarried and lives in the home keeps the exemption, and can move it to a later home. Every town's tax rate is in our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax calculator</a>.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How to apply, in order</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The exemption is not automatic. The SC Department of Revenue grants it, not the county auditor, and the order matters.</p><ol class="c3-va-steps"><li><strong>Get the 4 percent rate on your home.</strong>After closing, you apply to the Horry County Assessor for the 4 percent rate, the lower tax rate for the home you live in. The SC Department of Revenue will not grant the exemption until the county has.</li><li><strong>Get the disability certificate.</strong>It comes from the VA or from the county's veterans affairs office. A VA rating letter alone is not enough. <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/veterans-affairs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County Veterans Affairs</a> is at 1949 Industrial Park Road in Conway, and its phone is <a class="c3-va-nw" href="tel:+18439155480">(843) 915-5480</a>.</li><li><strong>Apply to the SC Department of Revenue.</strong>Apply online in <a href="https://mydorway.dor.sc.gov/?link=PT401I" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MyDORWAY</a>, or on Form PT-401-I. Send the recorded deed, the county's 4 percent approval and the certificate.</li><li><strong>Claim the whole year.</strong>A newly rated veteran can claim the exemption for the whole year the disability began, if they owned the home that year; if they bought it later, from the year they bought it. A late filer can go back up to two prior tax years if the taxes were paid on time.</li></ol><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Rated below 100 percent?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At 65, after a year living in South Carolina, the first $50,000 of your home's value is not taxed. It also applies if a state or federal agency has classified you totally and permanently disabled. You apply to the county auditor by July 15.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="appraisal"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The VA appraisal">What does the VA appraisal check?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Two things: what the home is worth, and whether it meets the VA's minimum property requirements, which your lender confirms.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">If the appraisal comes in low</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The VA loan cannot be more than the appraised value or the price, whichever is lower. The VA's own example: on a home under contract for $400,000 that appraises at $375,000, the loan is capped at $375,000. You then pay the gap in cash, the seller lowers the price, or the deal ends.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In our experience, low appraisals are rare here. When one comes in low, our agents gather comparable sales for a reconsideration of value, a request to look at the value again. Once the value changed and the buyer brought less to closing.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Homes built before 1978</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Older homes get one extra look. In a home built before 1978, the VA presumes lead paint, and any peeling or damaged paint must be fixed. Homes that old are far less common here than in the country as a whole.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes built before 1980, out of every 100"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes built before 1980, out of every 100</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Where</span><span role="columnheader">built before 1980</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Horry County</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.139" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">14 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">South Carolina</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.319" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">32 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">United States</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.481" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">48 in 100</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>U.S. Census Bureau, American Community Survey, all homes. The Census counts homes by the decade they were built, so 1980 is the closest line to 1978.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="closing"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Funding fee and closing costs">What does a VA buyer pay at closing?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A VA loan can need no down payment, as long as the price is not higher than the appraised value.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Unless you are exempt, you pay a one-time <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/funding-fee-and-closing-costs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA funding fee</a>. It is a share of the loan amount. The share drops if you make a large enough down payment. With little or no down payment, it is higher if you have used a VA loan before. You can add the fee to the loan or pay it at closing. On a purchase it is the only cost you can add to the loan.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Who pays no funding fee</h3><ul class="c3-va-cards" role="list" aria-label="Who pays no VA funding fee"><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span><strong>You get VA disability pay</strong>Or you are eligible for it but get retirement or active-duty pay instead.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>You are still serving and already rated</strong>Before your closing date, the VA rated you eligible for disability pay on a claim made before discharge.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>You are a surviving spouse with VA survivor pay</strong>Dependency and Indemnity Compensation (DIC), as the surviving spouse of a veteran.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>You are on active duty with a Purple Heart</strong>You show the lender proof of it on or before the closing date.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If the VA later awards you disability pay that starts before your closing date, you can ask for the funding fee back.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What the seller can pay</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A seller can pay all of your closing costs, with no VA limit. The VA's 4 percent limit is only for other help from the seller, such as paying your funding fee or paying off a debt. It is 4 percent of the value the VA appraisal gives the home.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Who pays the commission, the lender's fee for making the loan, the appraisal fee and title insurance is up to you and the seller. We write what you ask for into your offer. Our <a href="/buyers/closing-costs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">closing cost guide</a> lists each cost at closing in South Carolina.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="va-clinic"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The VA clinic">Where is the VA clinic in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Myrtle Beach VA Clinic is at 1800 Airpark Drive. It offers primary care, mental health and specialty care, and replaced two older clinics in town.</p><figure style="margin:1.4rem 0 .4rem;max-width:560px"><div class="c3-va-map"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic" viewBox="0 0 360 432" width="360" height="432" role="img" aria-label="Map of the Grand Strand with the Myrtle Beach VA Clinic and the drive to it from each town: Socastee about 10 minutes, Myrtle Beach about 12 minutes, Surfside Beach about 14 minutes, Carolina Forest about 20 minutes, Murrells Inlet about 20 minutes, Conway about 25 minutes, North Myrtle Beach about 35 minutes, Little River about 45 minutes, Loris about 55 minutes." style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:760px;background:#f7f3ec;border:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.15)"><style>#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic text{font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;paint-order:stroke;stroke:#f7f3ec;stroke-width:3px;stroke-linejoin:round;fill:#1c2028}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .h{font:500 17px 'Fraunces',Georgia,serif}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .l{font-size:14px;font-weight:500}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .m{font-size:13px;font-weight:500;fill:#91592b}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .t{font-size:14px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.1em;fill:#5c6b78}#c3r-myrtle-beach-va-clinic .T{font-size:14px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.1em;fill:#