coration-color:var(--brass);text-underline-offset:3px"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align:-3px;margin-right:.35rem"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5a7 7 0 0 1 14 0C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg>Open in Google Maps</a><a class="c3-map-link directions" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&amp;destination=33.677414,-78.945299" title="Directions to Myrtle Beach VA Clinic in Google Maps" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:var(--brass);text-underline-offset:3px"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align:-3px;margin-right:.35rem"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5a7 7 0 0 1 14 0C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg>Get directions</a></p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The clinic is part of the Ralph H. Johnson VA health care system. From the clinic, the nearest VA medical center is the Ralph H. Johnson VA Medical Center in Charleston, about 2 hours 10 minutes away without traffic. From Loris, Little River and North Myrtle Beach, the Fayetteville VA Medical Center in North Carolina is a shorter drive.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Military history here</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Warbird Park in Myrtle Beach keeps the history of the old Myrtle Beach Air Force Base, with a Wall of Service that lists people who served at the base.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:760px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-va-loans/warbird-park-jets-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-va-loans/warbird-park-jets-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/buyers-va-loans/warbird-park-jets-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 760px" width="1200" height="675" alt="Military jets in camouflage paint on display on a round plaza with small plaques, under tall pines at Warbird Park in Myrtle Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.loc.gov/rr/print/res/482_high.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Carol M. Highsmith. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Carol M. Highsmith</a></span></div><figcaption>Jets on display at Warbird Park in Myrtle Beach.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina does not tax military retirement pay, and a surviving spouse gets the same deduction. Our <a href="/buyers/retirees/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guide for retirees</a> covers the rest of the state's taxes on retirement income. Not every veteran here is retired. One of our clients is a veteran who lives here and works his New York job in alternating weeks.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="who-qualifies"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Who qualifies">Who qualifies for a VA loan, and how much can you borrow?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You need a Certificate of Eligibility (COE), the VA's letter that says you can use the benefit. These are the <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/eligibility/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">service minimums</a> for service from the Gulf War to today:</p><ul class="c3-va-cards" role="list" aria-label="VA loan service minimums"><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>Serving now</strong>90 days of active duty in a row.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>A veteran</strong>24 months in a row, or the full period you were called to active duty (at least 90 days), or less if discharged for a disability from your service.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5l5-3V21M10 21V4h9v17M13 8h3M13 12h3M13 16h3M7.5 13h.01M7.5 16.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>Guard and Reserve</strong>90 days of qualifying active duty, or 6 qualifying years if you still serve, left honorably or retired.</span></li><li><span class="c3-va-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>A surviving spouse</strong>If you get, or can get, certain VA survivor pay (DIC), or your spouse on active duty is missing in action or held as a prisoner of war.</span></li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much you can borrow</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Your entitlement is the most the VA will pay your lender if you do not repay the loan. Your COE shows your basic entitlement. The rest, for a larger loan, is worked out from the loan amount and is not on the COE. With your full entitlement there is <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-limits/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">no VA loan limit</a>: the lender decides how much you can borrow, and the appraisal must support the price.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you still have a VA loan on another home, part of your entitlement is in use. Your remaining entitlement is worked out from the county's loan limit, which is $832,750 for a one-unit home in Horry and Georgetown counties, minus the entitlement already in use. If what is left does not cover enough of the new loan, the lender may ask for a down payment.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Credit and down payment help</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The VA requires no minimum credit score, but some lenders have their own. SC Housing's VA loans with no down payment need a score of 640. SC Housing's year-round help works with a VA loan; our <a href="/buyers/programs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guide to SC Housing's programs</a> gives its limits.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="va-loan-questions"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">VA loan questions</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I use a VA loan more than once?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. After you sell the home and pay off the VA loan, you can ask the VA to restore your entitlement. With a VA loan still open on another home, you may have enough left for a second one.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I buy a manufactured home with a VA loan?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, if you will live in it. A VA loan can buy a manufactured home, or a lot for one. Few sellers here mark VA on them: about 15 in 100 manufactured homes for sale.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I buy a house with a tenant in it using a VA loan?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house with a tenant is hard to buy with a VA loan while a long lease runs, because you must be able to move in. Most lenders want you in the home within 60 days. We ask about the lease before you make an offer.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What interest rate will I get on a VA loan?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The lender quotes your rate. We do not quote rates. We can introduce you to our preferred lender, or you can use any lender you like.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://lgy.va.gov/lgyhub/condo-report" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA condo report</a>, <a href="https://entp.hud.gov/idapp/html/condlook.cfm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD FHA condo list</a>, <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/purchase-loan/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA purchase loans</a>, <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/funding-fee-and-closing-costs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA funding fee</a>, <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-limits/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA loan limits</a>, <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/eligibility/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA eligibility</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c037.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-37</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/PT401I.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR PT-401-I</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County 2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.va.gov/charleston-health-care/locations/myrtle-beach-va-clinic/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Beach VA Clinic</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDT1Y2024.B25034?g=050XX00US45051" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census ACS</a>. Homes for sale: Chapter3's count of MLS listings, in aggregate; a community's condos are matched by its name and checked against its street. Drive times: OpenStreetMap routing, no traffic. Not loan or tax advice.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Warbird Park in Myrtle Beach. Photo: Carol M. Highsmith, <a href="https://www.loc.gov/rr/print/res/482_high.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://www.loc.gov/item/2017880876/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Library of Congress</a>. Chapter3 Realty cropped the left side and the top of this photo to a 16:9 frame and resized it.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/buyers-va-loans/warbird-park-jets-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/buyers-va-loans/warbird-park-jets-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":675,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"Jets on display at Warbird Park in Myrtle Beach","caption":"Jets on display at Warbird Park in Myrtle Beach.","description":"Military jets in camouflage paint on display on a round plaza with small plaques, under tall pines at Warbird Park in Myrtle Beach","creator":{"@type":"Person","name":"Carol M. Highsmith"},"creditText":"Carol M. Highsmith","copyrightNotice":"Public domain (Carol M. Highsmith)","license":"https://www.loc.gov/rr/print/res/482_high.html","acquireLicensePage":"https://www.loc.gov/item/2017880876/","isBasedOn":"https://www.loc.gov/item/2017880876/","contentLocation":{"@type":"Place","name":"Warbird Park, Myrtle Beach, South Carolina"},"representativeOfPage":true}]}</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Send us the home you like</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">For a condo, we look up its community. For a house, we ask whether the seller takes VA. Then we show you the homes you pick.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Ask about a home</a></div></section></main>
+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">VA Loans</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Military and veterans</p><h1 class="detail-h1">VA loans in Myrtle Beach:<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">which condos and homes qualify.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 3, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Your VA loan can buy most kinds of home here, but a condo must be in one of about 175 Horry County communities on the VA's list.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You can use a VA loan on a house you will live in, if the seller agrees and the house passes the VA appraisal. The appraisal is the VA's check of the home's value and condition. About half the houses for sale on the Grand Strand are marked as taking a VA loan. A condo needs a community on the VA's list, and few oceanfront resort towers are on it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If the VA rates you permanently and totally disabled from your service, you pay no property tax on your home. On a home the county values at $400,000, that saves about $1,470 to $2,610 a year.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Send us a condo or a house you like. We find out whether a VA loan can buy it before you tour.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Ask about a home</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#which-homes" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which homes qualify</a></li><li><a href="#va-approved-condos" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">VA-approved condos</a></li><li><a href="#sellers" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Sellers who take VA</a></li><li><a href="#second-homes" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Second homes and rentals</a></li><li><a href="#property-tax" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Property tax exemption</a></li><li><a href="#appraisal" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The VA appraisal</a></li><li><a href="#closing" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Funding fee and closing costs</a></li><li><a href="#va-clinic" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The VA clinic</a></li><li><a href="#who-qualifies" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Who qualifies</a></li><li><a href="#va-loan-questions" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">VA loan questions</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="which-homes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Which homes qualify">Can you use a VA loan on the home you want in Myrtle Beach?</h2><style id="c3-glass">main#main{--g-ink:#8a5226;--g-ink-lg:#a8612c;--g-edge:rgba(255,255,255,.8);--g-hi:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.95);--g-sh:0 1px 2px rgba(28,32,40,.05),0 14px 36px -20px rgba(28,32,40,.3);--g-r:20px;--g-blur:saturate(150%) blur(16px);background-color:#f8f4ee;background-image:radial-gradient(44rem 26rem at 4% 460px,rgba(232,201,154,.30),rgba(232,201,154,0) 70%),radial-gradient(40rem 26rem at 98% 1000px,rgba(196,120,58,.08),rgba(196,120,58,0) 70%),radial-gradient(46rem 26rem at 16% 1500px,rgba(232,201,154,.22),rgba(232,201,154,0) 70%),radial-gradient(40rem 24rem at 94% 1960px,rgba(42,48,64,.045),rgba(42,48,64,0) 70%);background-size:100% 2400px;background-repeat:repeat-y}main#main>section[style*="background:var(--ivory"],main#main .detail-hero{background:transparent!important}main#main .detail-hero{border-bottom:0}main#main .detail-hero.bg-grid{background-image:none}main#main>section[style*="background:var(--ivory"]+section[style*="background:var(--ivory"]{border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.7)}main#main>section[style*="background:var(--ivory"]{padding-bottom:2.25rem}main#main>section[style*="background:var(--ivory"]:not(.detail-hero+section){padding