w it</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">You need an FHA or VA loan</th><td data-label="The better choice">Most likely a house</td><td data-label="Why">Horry County has 9 FHA-approved ones</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">You may need to sell within a few years</th><td data-label="The better choice">A house</td><td data-label="Why">Condos sit longer; houses sell sooner</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">You do not want to manage a roof, a pool or the building's insurance</th><td data-label="The better choice">A condo</td><td data-label="Why">The HOA takes care of the building</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The rest depends on the building: its fee, its rules and whether a lender will finance it. The <a href="#the-building" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">building section</a> below lists what decides one.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="prices-over-time"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Prices over time">How have Myrtle Beach condo prices done compared with houses?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From its 2006 high to early 2012, the typical metro condo lost about 43 percent of its value. The typical house lost about 30 percent.</p><figure class="c3-gchart c3-cd-fig"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .5rem">Typical condo and house value, Myrtle Beach metro</span><ul class="c3-cd-legend"><li><span class="c3-cd-line" style="background:#2f6f8f"></span>Houses</li><li><span class="c3-cd-line" style="background:#c4783a"></span>Condos</li></ul><svg class="c3-cd-chart" viewBox="0 0 360 262" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of the typical home value in the Myrtle Beach metro, monthly from late 2001 to September 2026. Condos rose from about $112,000 to a high of about $197,000 in November 2006, fell to about $113,000 in January 2012, rose to about $261,000 in October 2023 and were about $231,000 in September 2026. Houses rose from about $146,000 to about $364,000, and fell less after 2007."><rect x="56" y="30" width="240" height="192" fill="rgba(255,255,255,.55)" rx="6"/><line x1="56" y1="158" x2="296" y2="158" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text class="ct" x="50" y="163" text-anchor="end">$200k</text><line x1="56" y1="94" x2="296" y2="94" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text class="ct" x="50" y="99" text-anchor="end">$300k</text><line x1="56" y1="30" x2="296" y2="30" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text class="ct" x="50" y="35" text-anchor="end">$400k</text><text class="ct" x="50" y="227" text-anchor="end">$100k</text><text class="ct" x="57.6" y="246" text-anchor="middle">2002</text><text class="ct" x="134.9" y="246" text-anchor="middle">2010</text><text class="ct" x="212.2" y="246" text-anchor="middle">2018</text><text class="ct" x="289.6" y="246" text-anchor="middle">2026</text><path d="M56 192.3L56.8 192.2L57.6 192.1L58.4 192.2L59.2 192.2L60 192.4L60.8 192.3L61.6 192.2L62.4 191.8L63.2 191.4L64.1 191L64.9 190.7L65.7 190.4L66.5 190.1L67.3 189.7L68.1 189.3L68.9 189L69.7 188.8L70.5 188.6L71.3 188.5L72.1 188.2L72.9 187.8L73.7 187.3L74.5 186.8L75.3 186.3L76.1 185.7L76.9 185.1L77.7 184.3L78.6 183.6L79.4 182.8L80.2 182L81 181.1L81.8 180L82.6 179.1L83.4 178.1L84.2 176.9L85 175.6L85.8 174.4L86.6 172.9L87.4 171.2L88.2 169.2L89 167.5L89.8 165.9L90.6 164.3L91.4 162.4L92.2 160.3L93 158.1L93.9 155.9L94.7 153.6L95.5 151.3L96.3 149.4L97.1 147.3L97.9 145.1L98.7 142.9L99.5 140.8L100.3 139.1L101.1 137.1L101.9 135.4L102.7 133.8L103.5 132.2L104.3 131.4L105.1 131L105.9 130.9L106.7 130.7L107.5 130.5L108.3 130.4L109.2 130.2L110 130.2L110.8 130.5L111.6 130.8L112.4 131.4L113.2 132.2L114 133.1L114.8 133.7L115.6 133.8L116.4 134.1L117.2 134.9L118 135.7L118.8 136.6L119.6 137.1L12