 font-weight="600" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">value</text><text x="652.0" y="95.0" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="#8a5226" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">rent</text></svg><div class="rp-tabwrap"><table class="rp-tab"><caption>A house's asking rent and value each September</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Year</th><th scope="col">Rent a month</th><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">A year's rent as a share of value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2019</td><td>$1,380</td><td>$234K</td><td>7.1%</td></tr><tr><td>2022</td><td>$1,910</td><td>$366K</td><td>6.3%</td></tr><tr><td>2026</td><td>$2,070</td><td>$364K</td><td>6.8%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figcaption>Zillow's rent index for houses and Zillow's middle-tier house value index, Myrtle Beach metro, September of each year to September 2026. A year's rent is twelve months of the asking rent, before any cost; it is not a return.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Over the last four years, the asking rent for a house rose about 8 percent while the house value stayed about flat. A year's rent is now a larger share of the price than it was. Since 2019, both rose by about half.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For one address, we add the tax, HOA dues and insurance to see whether today's rent pays them: <a href="/invest/run-the-numbers/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">how we run the numbers on a rental</a>. <a href="/invest/where-to-buy/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Where to buy a rental</a> compares the parts of the Grand Strand by strategy.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="best-month"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Best month">When is the best month to rent out a house in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Summer. Asking rents are about half a percent above the year's trend in August, the high, and about 1.4 percent below it in January, the low. A year's lease that starts in summer also ends in summer, so you look for the next tenant in the high months too.</p><figure class="c3-gchart rp-fig"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .8rem">Asking rents each month, above or below the year's trend</span><svg class="rp-n" viewBox="0 0 280 174" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart of asking rents against the year's trend, by month. Rents are above the trend from June to October, highest in August, about half a percent above. They are below it from November to April, lowest in January, about 1.4 percent below."><line x1="42" x2="274" y1="22.4" y2="22.4" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="36" y="27.3" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">+1%</text><line x1="42" x2="274" y1="69.9" y2="69.9" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".45"/><text x="36" y="74.8" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">trend</text><line x1="42" x2="274" y1="117.5" y2="117.5" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="36" y="122.4" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">−1%</text><rect x="45.7" y="69.9" width="12.0" height="64.2" rx="3" fill="#7d8291"><title>January</title></rect><text x="51.7" y="150.2" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">low</text><text x="51.7" y="168.4" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">J</text><rect x="65.0" y="69.9" width="12.0" height="49.9" rx="3" fill="#7d8291"><title>February</title></rect><text x="71.0" y="168.4" text-anchor="middle" font-s