 apartments and condos with houses. Across the metro area, the asking rent for a house is about $350 a month higher than for every home together.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/invest-rent-prices/carolina-forest-streets-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/invest-rent-prices/carolina-forest-streets-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/invest-rent-prices/carolina-forest-streets-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 680px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Rows of houses with gray roofs and short driveways along streets with strips of woods between them in Carolina Forest, seen from above" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses in Carolina Forest, seen from above. Carolina Forest is in ZIP code 29579, row 5 of the table.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="up-or-down"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Are rents rising">Is rent going up or down in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Up. Asking rents for houses rose about 3 percent in the last year, to the highest point in Zillow's index.</p><figure class="c3-gchart rp-fig"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .8rem">House rent and house value, change since 2015</span><ul class="rp-key" aria-hidden="true"><li><i style="background:#c4783a"></i>House asking rent</li><li><i style="background:repeating-linear-gradient(90deg,#1c2028 0 6px,transparent 6px 10px)"></i>House value</li></ul><svg class="rp-n" viewBox="0 0 280 218" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of two Zillow indexes for the Myrtle Beach metro, September of each year from 2015 to 2026, as the change since 2015. The asking rent for a house and the middle-tier house value both rose steeply from 2020 to 2022. Over the last four years the rent kept rising, about 8 percent, while the house value stayed about flat."><rect x="189.6" y="8.4" width="76.4" height="177.4" fill="#c4783a" fill-opacity=".09" rx="6"/><text x="227.8" y="175.1" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">last 4 years</text><line x1="56" x2="266" y1="185.8" y2="185.8" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".3"/><text x="50" y="190.7" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">0</text><line x1="56" x2="266" y1="143.6" y2="143.6" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="50" y="148.5" text-anchor="end