 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Conway, SC a good place to live?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For a buyer who wants a river town with a downtown and a university, at prices under the county's middle, yes. The trade is the drive: the beach is about 25 minutes away by car."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How far is Conway from Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About 25 minutes by car from downtown Conway to the beach in Myrtle Beach, without traffic, and about 27 minutes to Myrtle Beach International Airport."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Conway, SC flood?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In a few places. About 95 in 100 homes in the city are outside both FEMA's high-risk zone and the land Florence's water reached; most of the rest are near the Waccamaw River, Crabtree Swamp and Kingston Lake."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the property tax rate in Conway, SC?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Inside the city, a home you live in pays about $654 a year for every $100,000 of the county's value for it. Just outside the city, it pays about $368, plus an $89 county stormwater fee. A second home or rental pays about 2.5 times as much inside the city."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many people live in Conway, SC?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About 30,600 in 2025, by the Census Bureau's estimate, up from 24,849 at the 2020 Census."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Conway, SC safe?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We do not rate any place as safe or unsafe. Inside the city limits, the City of Conway has its own police department and fire department."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which schools serve Conway, SC?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Horry County Schools assigns schools by address, and one of its attendance areas is named Conway. We look up the assigned schools for any house you like."}}]}</script>
