mons","copyrightNotice":"© LittleT889, CC BY-SA 4.0","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","acquireLicensePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kimbel_Library.jpg","isBasedOn":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kimbel_Library.jpg","contentLocation":{"@type":"Place","name":"Coastal Carolina University, Conway, South Carolina"},"representativeOfPage":true},{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-10-d/buyers-undisclosed-flooding/conway-florence-floodwater-street-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-10-d/buyers-undisclosed-flooding/conway-florence-floodwater-street-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":844,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"Floodwater on a street of houses in the Conway area after Florence","caption":"Floodwater on a street of houses in the Conway area after Florence.","description":"Floodwater covering a street and the yards of single-story houses, with road signs standing in the water, in the Conway area after Hurricane Florence","creator":{"@type":"Person","name":"Senior Master Sgt. Edward Snyder, 169th Fighter Wing, South Carolina National Guard"},"creditText":"South Carolina National Guard (Senior Master Sgt","copyrightNotice":"Public domain (Senior Master Sgt. Edward Snyder, 169th Fighter Wing, South Carolina National Guard)","license":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Template:PD-USGov-Military-National_Guard","acquireLicensePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hurricane_Florence_-_South_Carolina_National_Guard_Responds_(44200296354).jpg","isBasedOn":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hurricane_Florence_-_South_Carolina_National_Guard_Responds_(44200296354).jpg","contentLocation":{"@type":"Place","name":"Conway area, South Carolina (the source does not name the street), Conway, South Carolina"},"representativeOfPage":true}]}</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Tell us the street. We will tell you what it means.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">Send us any Conway house you like. We tell you whether it is inside the city, whether it is in either flood map, and what its yearly tax will be.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/?place=Conway">Ask about a Conway house</a></div></section></main>
+</style><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway is a small city on the Waccamaw River, said WAH-kuh-maw. Much of downtown was built in the early 1900s, after a fire, and its streets have old live oaks.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Riverwalk is a path of about 1.5 miles along the river, with benches and a kayak launch. It starts about 3 minutes by car from the center of town. At Riverfront Park beside it are a public boat landing with floating docks, a playground built like an old river steamboat, and rocking chairs under a gazebo.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A wooden boardwalk with a black railing under tall sycamores, beside old wooden buildings on the river in Conway" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>The boardwalk along the Waccamaw River, at the edge of downtown Conway.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway was laid out in 1732, as Kingston, and later named Conwayborough for General Robert Conway of the state militia.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">City Hall on Main Street was finished in 1825 as the county courthouse. Its design is credited to Robert Mills, who designed the Washington Monument.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/conway-city-hall-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/conway-city-hall-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/conway-city-hall-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="800" alt="Conway City Hall, a brick building with a white portico of four columns and stairs up both sides, beside a white clock tower and palmetto trees" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pollinator at en.wikipedia. License: CC BY-SA 3.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 3.0">Photo: Pollinator at en.wikipedia</a></span></div><figcaption>Conway City Hall on Main Street, once the county courthouse.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Coastal Carolina University is inside the city, about 10 minutes from downtown. It enrolled more than 11,000 students in fall 2024, a record for the school. Horry-Georgetown Technical College has its Conway campus on US 501, and Conway Medical Center is about 10 minutes from downtown.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city is growing fast. By Census estimates it grew about 22 percent since 2020, the seventh fastest among South Carolina cities and towns of 10,000 people or more.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The beach is about 25 minutes away by car, and the airport about 27.</p><figure class="c3-cw-fig" style="max-width:560px"><div class="c3-cw-frame"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="c3r-downtown-conway" viewBox="0 0 360 380" width="360" height="380" role="img" aria-label="Map of Conway and the coast: from downtown Conway, the beach in Myrtle Beach is about 25 minu