iddle">Atlantic Ocean</text><circle cx="853.7" cy="1261.7" r="15" fill="#fff" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="5"/><text class="lb" x="877.7" y="1239.7" text-anchor="start">MarshWalk</text><g transform="translate(641.7 672.7)"><circle r="54" fill="#2f6f8f" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="8"/><text class="pn" y="26" text-anchor="middle">1</text></g><g transform="translate(385 1331)"><circle r="54" fill="#5f8a4e" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="8"/><text class="pn" y="26" text-anchor="middle">2</text></g><g transform="translate(698.8 1373)"><circle r="54" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="8"/><text class="pn" y="26" text-anchor="middle">3</text></g><line x1="875" y1="1485" x2="746.7" y2="1373" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="6"/><circle cx="746.7" cy="1373" r="9" fill="#fff"/><g transform="translate(875 1485)"><circle r="54" fill="#8a4fa0" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="8"/><text class="pn" y="26" text-anchor="middle">4</text></g></svg></div><figcaption>The dashed line is the county line. The shading covers where the homes are. Aerial photo: USGS, public domain. County line, roads and home locations: U.S. Census Bureau, Horry and Georgetown counties and OpenStreetMap contributors.</figcaption><ol class="c3-mi-key" aria-label="The four parts of Murrells Inlet"><li><span class="c3-mi-num p1" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span><b style="color:var(--navy)">The Horry side</b>: golf neighborhoods and most of the homes</span></li><li><span class="c3-mi-num p2" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span><b style="color:var(--navy)">Georgetown, west of the bypass</b>: Wachesaw, golf and the river landing</span></li><li><span class="c3-mi-num p3" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span><b style="color:var(--navy)">Between the bypass and Business 17</b>: streets in the middle of the village</span></li><li><span class="c3-mi-num p4" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span><b style="color:var(--navy)">The creek side</b>: houses on the salt marsh, and the MarshWalk</span></li></ol></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="parts"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Four parts">Where should you buy in Murrells Inlet?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each of the four parts is a different way to live here. The numbers match the map above.</p><h3 id="horry-side" data-toc="The Horry side" class="c3-mi-h3"><span class="c3-mi-num p1" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span>The Horry side: golf neighborhoods and most of the homes</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most Murrells Inlet homes are here, north of the county line and west of the US 17 bypass. The neighborhoods are laid out around golf courses and ponds: the International Club, Blackmoor, the TPC of Myrtle Beach and Indigo Creek's course are all on this side.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The largest house neighborhoods are Indigo Creek, with about 560 houses, Seasons at Prince Creek West (a <a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">55+ community</a>), The Pines of St. James and Longwood Bluffs. Clients of ours sold their house in Blackmoor, a golf community with no age restriction, to buy in Seasons at Prince Creek West, an age-restricted community a few minutes away.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-horry-side-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-horry-side-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-horry-side-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of the Horry side of Murrells Inlet: houses on curving streets and cul-de-sacs beside golf fairways, sand bunkers, ponds and woods, with rows of townhouses at the lower left" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The Horry side from above: houses on curving streets beside the ponds and fairways of the Indigo Creek golf course.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Publix and Lowes Foods are on SC 707, about 4 minutes from the middle of this side. The MarshWalk is about 9 minutes away.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Almost every house for sale here is in an HOA (homeowners association), and the middle fee was about $110 a month. Most of the <a href="/buyers/no-hoa-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">houses with no HOA</a> are on the Georgetown side. About 1 in 9 houses sold here in the past year was new from a builder. Townhouses and condos cost less, about $320,000 and $275,000.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Murrells%20Inlet&amp;part=horry-side">Send me Horry-side homes in Murrells Inlet<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="georgetown-west" data-toc="Georgetown, west of the bypass" class="c3-mi-h3"><span class="c3-mi-num p2" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span>Georgetown, west of the bypass: Wachesaw, golf and the river</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South of the county line and west of the bypass, the land runs down to the Waccamaw River. Boats go in at Wacca Wache Landing, off Wachesaw Road. On the river, the tide rises and falls about half as much as in the inlet.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-wacca-wache-landing-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-wacca-wache-landing-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-wacca-wache-landing-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of the Waccamaw River off Wachesaw Road, labelled: the dark river, Wacca Wache Landing on its bank, a marina basin full of boats, and woods and buildings around it" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Wacca Wache Landing on the Waccamaw River, with a marina beside it, on the Georgetown side west of the bypass.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The largest neighborhood is <a href="/buyers/gated-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Wachesaw Plantation</a>, with about 650 houses, then Linksbrook and Collins Creek. The Wachesaw Plantation Club and Wachesaw East golf courses are on this side. Prince Creek crosses the county line: Palm Bay is in Georgetown County, Seasons at Prince Creek West is in Horry, and Highwood is split between them.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The middle HOA fee on houses for sale here was about $150 a month.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Murrells%20Inlet&amp;part=georgetown-west">Send me Georgetown-side homes in Murrells Inlet<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="between-the-roads" data-toc="Between the bypass and Business 17" class="c3-mi-h3"><span class="c3-mi-num p3" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span>Between the bypass and Business 17: streets in the middle of the village</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">This narrow band is on the Georgetown side, between the US 17 bypass and Business 17. It has about 800 homes on streets of houses like the ones in the photo. Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital and a Food Lion are just west of the bypass. The MarshWalk, the restaurants and the creek are just east of Business 17.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-between-the-roads-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-between-the-roads-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-between-the-roads-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of Murrells Inlet, labelled: the US 17 bypass at the left with shops along it, Business 17 at the right, and streets of houses between them, with a loop street of newer houses in the middle" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Between the US 17 bypass and Business 17 from above: streets of houses, with a loop street of newer houses in the middle and shops along the bypass at the left.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house here sold for about $530,000 at the middle in the past year, and a condo or villa for about $280,000. Some streets here are in FEMA's high-risk flood zone and some are not, so we look up the zone for each house before you offer.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Murrells%20Inlet&amp;part=between-the-roads">Send me homes between the highways in Murrells Inlet<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="creek-side" data-toc="The creek side" class="c3-mi-h3"><span class="c3-mi-num p4" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span>The creek side: houses on the salt marsh</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">East of Business 17, on the Georgetown side, houses line the edge of the inlet's salt marsh, many with a dock out to the creek. This is where the village began, and it is a National Register historic district. The county's named areas here include Sunnyside, the Hermitage and Vaux Hall. The MarshWalk's restaurants are on this side.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-creek-front-docks-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-creek-front-docks-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-creek-front-docks-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of creek-front houses in Murrells Inlet, labelled: Business 17 at the left, houses under live oaks, and wooden docks running from the yards out to the tidal creek, with salt marsh islands beyond" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses on the creek side of Business 17 from above, with docks reaching out over the marsh edge to the creek.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The creek side has about 370 homes. About 220 of them are houses on the edge of the marsh, and few of those come up for sale: 21 sold in the past three years. The middle one sold for about $930,000, about 1.7 times the middle house west of the bypass over the same years.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Murrells%20Inlet&amp;part=creek-side">Send me creek-front homes in Murrells Inlet<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="life"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Daily life">What is it like to live in Murrells Inlet?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The <a href="https://marshwalk.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MarshWalk</a> is a half-mile wooden boardwalk along the salt marsh, lined with restaurants such as Drunken Jack's, Dead Dog Saloon, Creek Ratz and The Wicked Tuna. Its live music is free to hear. Crazy Sister Marina and the county's Murrells Inlet boat landing are at its south end.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-marshwalk-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-marshwalk-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-marshwalk-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of the MarshWalk in Murrells Inlet, labelled: restaurant buildings and decks along a boardwalk at the edge of the inlet, Business 17 behind them, marsh islands in the creek and a marina with boats at the bottom" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The MarshWalk from above: restaurants along the boardwalk at the edge of the inlet, Business 17 behind them, and salt marsh islands in the creek.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 85 in 100 houses outside Garden City are taxed as their owner's main home.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Oysters in season</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From October 1 into May, you can gather oysters and clams on the inlet's three public shellfish grounds with a South Carolina saltwater fishing license. They are the state grounds named Murrells Inlet and Drunken Jack Island, and a public ground at the old Lachicotte oyster factory. A resident's license costs $15 a year, and no license is needed under 16. There is a daily limit, on no more than two days in any seven, and parts of each ground are closed by the state.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The beach, groceries and the hospital</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The creek side has no ocean beach. The nearest are <a href="https://southcarolinaparks.com/huntington-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Huntington Beach State Park</a>, about 9 minutes from the MarshWalk, with 3 miles of beach and a freshwater lake known for alligators, and Garden City Beach, about 9 minutes away.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the Horry side, Publix and Lowes Foods are on SC 707 and a Walmart Neighborhood Market is on the US 17 bypass. On the Georgetown side, a Food Lion is on the bypass near the hospital. Two of our own team chose to live in Murrells Inlet. One of them drives from here to Market Common and to a gym in Carolina Forest.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">From the MarshWalk to</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">By car, about</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">4 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Brookgreen Gardens</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">12 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/submarkets/pawleys-island/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Pawleys Island</a></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">15 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Market Common</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach International Airport</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">25 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Broadway at the Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">25 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Charleston</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">2 hours</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Times are without traffic. Summer traffic on US 17 adds time.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="docks"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Docks and tides">Can a creek-front house in Murrells Inlet have a dock?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Usually. South Carolina allows one dock per lot on the salt marsh, if the lot has enough marsh frontage and the creek in front of it is wide enough. Before you offer on a creek-front house, we pull the dock's permit and check the frontage and the creek's width.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Few houses for sale have a dock. Of the 465 listings with a Murrells Inlet address, Garden City included, listing agents marked a private dock on 9. Only 2 of those were on the creek side. A creek house with a dock does come up, but you may wait for one.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much water is at the dock?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The tide in the inlet rises and falls about 4 feet on an average day, at NOAA's prediction station at Captain Alex's Marina. About 3 low tides in 10 drop below the low-water mark on the creek's charts. At a dock with little water, a boat can sit on the mud at those tides. We look at the dock at low tide before you offer. Our <a href="/buyers/waterfront-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">waterfront homes guide</a> covers what else to look at.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where can you launch a boat?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Georgetown County lists four boat landings in the Murrells Inlet ZIP code. The Murrells Inlet Landing is at the MarshWalk, Marina Colony is on Business 17 and Morse Landing is at the inlet's south end. Wacca Wache Landing is on the Waccamaw River.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="property-tax"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Property tax">What are property taxes in Murrells Inlet?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the same house, the bill is higher on the Georgetown side. For a $450,000 house, the yearly tax is about:</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase"></th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Horry</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Georgetown</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Main home</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,860</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$2,420</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Second home or rental</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$5,690</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$6,900</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Parts 3 and 4 on the map are on the Georgetown side. A new owner's bill is figured on the price paid, and your HOA fee and homeowners insurance come on top. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax calculator</a> has the rate for every part of both counties.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="flooding"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flooding">Does Murrells Inlet flood?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Few homes west of the US 17 bypass are in FEMA's high-risk flood zone. Most homes on the creek side are. In that zone, a lender requires flood insurance.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, by part of Murrells Inlet"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, by part of Murrells Inlet</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Part</span><span role="columnheader">Homes in the zone</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1. The Horry side</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.018" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 2 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2. Georgetown, west of the bypass</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.016" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 2 in 100</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">3. Between the bypass and Business 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.348" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 3</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">4. The creek side</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.858" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 6 in 7</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Every home's flood zone on the county's FEMA map, at the middle of its lot. The numbers match the map above.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the creek side, about 1 in 9 of the houses on the marsh are in FEMA's V zone, where waves are expected in a big storm. A flood policy costs the most there.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What flood insurance costs here</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The middle federal flood policy on a house cost about $590 a year on the Georgetown side and about $580 on the Horry side. On the Georgetown side, a house in FEMA's A zone, the high-risk zone away from the waves, paid about $1,080. A house in the V zone, where FEMA expects waves, paid about $2,160.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most of the flood policies on Georgetown-side houses are on homes outside the high-risk zone. Before you offer, we pull the flood zone and an insurance quote for the house. Our pages on <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance</a> and <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">finding out whether a house has flooded</a> show what we look at.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="renting"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Renting">Can you rent out a house in Murrells Inlet?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It depends on the HOA papers and the county zoning for that lot. An HOA can forbid or limit rentals in its papers, and almost every Horry-side house for sale is in one. We read the HOA papers and check the zoning before you offer.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the Horry side, the county asks a nightly-rental owner for a business license and tax filings, and names no rental permit. Guests pay about 12 percent in lodging taxes. On the Georgetown side, the county issues no business license, and guests pay about 11 percent. The details are on our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules page</a> and our <a href="/invest/accommodations-tax/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">accommodations tax page</a>.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What a Murrells Inlet Airbnb earns</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">AirROI, a company that tracks Airbnb listings, counts about 480 active listings in Murrells Inlet. Its count may take in Garden City Beach homes with a Murrells Inlet address. The average listing took in about $47,600 in gross bookings in the past 12 months, before costs. Most of that comes in summer.</p><figure class="c3-gchart c3-mi-fig"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .5rem">What a Murrells Inlet Airbnb earns in an average month</span><svg class="c3-mi-cols" viewBox="0 0 360 236" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Column chart of what a Murrells Inlet Airbnb earns in an average month: Jan $2,250, Feb $2,660, Mar $4,310, Apr $5,220, May $6,030, Jun $9,300, Jul $9,780, Aug $6,840, Sep $4,490, Oct $3,900, Nov $3,020, Dec $2,980."><line x1="70" x2="352" y1="200" y2="200" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="64" y="205" text-anchor="end">$0</text><line x1="70" x2="352" y1="120.9" y2="120.9" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".12"/><text x="64" y="125.9" text-anchor="end">$5,000</text><line x1="70" x2="352" y1="41.8" y2="41.8" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".12"/><text x="64" y="46.8" text-anchor="end">$10,000</text><rect x="73.3" y="164.4" width="16.9" height="35.6" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="81.8" y="222" text-anchor="middle">J</text><text class="v" x="91.8" y="156.4" text-anchor="middle">$2,250</text><rect x="96.8" y="157.9" width="16.9" height="42.1" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="105.3" y="222" text-anchor="middle">F</text><rect x="120.3" y="131.8" width="16.9" height="68.2" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="128.8" y="222" text-anchor="middle">M</text><rect x="143.8" y="117.4" width="16.9" height="82.6" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="152.3" y="222" text-anchor="middle">A</text><rect x="167.3" y="104.6" width="16.9" height="95.4" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="175.8" y="222" text-anchor="middle">M</text><rect x="190.8" y="52.9" width="16.9" height="147.1" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="199.3" y="222" text-anchor="middle">J</text><rect x="214.3" y="45.3" width="16.9" height="154.7" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="222.8" y="222" text-anchor="middle">J</text><text class="v" x="222.8" y="37.3" text-anchor="middle">$9,780</text><rect x="237.8" y="91.8" width="16.9" height="108.2" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="246.3" y="222" text-anchor="middle">A</text><rect x="261.3" y="129" width="16.9" height="71" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="269.8" y="222" text-anchor="middle">S</text><rect x="284.8" y="138.3" width="16.9" height="61.7" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="293.3" y="222" text-anchor="middle">O</text><rect x="308.3" y="152.2" width="16.9" height="47.8" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="316.8" y="222" text-anchor="middle">N</text><rect x="331.8" y="152.9" width="16.9" height="47.1" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="340.3" y="222" text-anchor="middle">D</text></svg><figcaption>AirROI's average per active listing over two years, before cleaning, fees and management. Darker columns are May to August, the high season.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Worked example: nightly renting against a yearly lease</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The gap between a typical Airbnb and a yearly lease grows with the size of the house. The table compares a typical Airbnb of each size with a year's lease at HUD's fair rent, the government's figure for a standard rental in the ZIP code, rent and utilities included.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>A Murrells Inlet Airbnb against a yearly lease at HUD's fair rent</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Home size</th><th scope="col">Typical Airbnb, a year, before costs</th><th scope="col">HUD's fair rent, 12 months</th><th scope="col">The gap, before costs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">2 bedrooms</th><td data-label="Typical Airbnb, a year, before costs">$27,500</td><td data-label="HUD's fair rent, 12 months">$20,640</td><td data-label="The gap, before costs">About $6,900 more</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3 bedrooms</th><td data-label="Typical Airbnb, a year, before costs">$30,600</td><td data-label="HUD's fair rent, 12 months">$24,960</td><td data-label="The gap, before costs">About $5,600 more</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4 bedrooms</th><td data-label="Typical Airbnb, a year, before costs">$54,100</td><td data-label="HUD's fair rent, 12 months">$29,040</td><td data-label="The gap, before costs">About $25,000 more</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Airbnb figures are before cleaning, platform fees, management, furniture and utilities. Rents by area are on our <a href="/invest/rent-prices/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rent prices page</a>, and our <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">long-term rental analyzer</a> and <a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Airbnb income page</a> run both sides for one house. Selling a rental to buy here? Our <a href="/invest/strategies/1031-exchange/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">1031 exchange guide</a> covers the tax.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Thinking of renting a Murrells Inlet house?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We read the HOA papers on renting, check the zoning, and price the tax, the flood policy and the fees for that house.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask about a Murrells Inlet rental</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="history"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="History">How did Murrells Inlet become a seafood village?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Murrells Inlet began with the homes of two rice planters. Around 1850, Sunnyside was built for Jacob Motte Alston, and the Hermitage for Dr. Allard Belin Flagg, the master of Wachesaw plantation, on the edge of the marsh. A small settlement grew up along the marsh on their old lands.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/sunnyside-murrells-inlet-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/sunnyside-murrells-inlet-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/sunnyside-murrells-inlet-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="675" alt="Sunnyside in Murrells Inlet: a white one-and-a-half-story cottage with a front gable, a porch on four square columns, two brick chimneys and a red door, with live oaks around a lawn" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Upstateherd. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: Upstateherd</a></span></div><figcaption>Sunnyside, built about 1850, one of the two planters' houses the creek-side village grew from.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Visitors first came for oyster roasts and fried shore dinners put on by the inlet's founding families, the Morses, Nances, Vereens, Olivers, Chandlers and Lees. That grew into the restaurants that earned the nickname "Seafood Capital." Hurricane Hugo struck the creek front in 1989, and the village rebuilt.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Georgetown County plans to dredge the inlet's creeks. In <a href="https://dph.sc.gov/sites/scdph/files/media/document/Special-Appropriations/Special-Appropriations-Q4-2024/Q4ExpRpt-Georgetown-County-Murrells-Inlet-Dredging.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">a report to the state</a>, it estimated the cost at about $30 million.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="murrells-inlet-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Murrells Inlet FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What ZIP code is Murrells Inlet?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">29576. It covers the Horry side, the Georgetown side and Garden City, so the ZIP code does not tell you the county.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Murrells Inlet part of Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. No part of the Murrells Inlet ZIP code is inside Myrtle Beach or any other town.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does Murrells Inlet have a beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not on the creek side. Huntington Beach State Park and Garden City Beach are the nearest beaches.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What schools serve Murrells Inlet?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry-side homes are zoned for the St. James schools of Horry County Schools. Georgetown-side homes are zoned for the Waccamaw schools of the Georgetown County School District. We look up the assigned schools for any home you like.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://data.census.gov/table?g=160XX00US4548985" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census 2020</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry GIS</a>, <a href="https://gis1.georgetowncountysc.org/portal/rest/services" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgetown GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry deeds</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry 2026 levy</a>, <a href="https://www.gtcountysc.gov/385/Property-Tax-Calculator" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgetown tax estimate</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/fima-nfip-redacted-policies-v2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenFEMA</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/monjnvh0/sales-tax-chart-short-term-rentals.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry STR filings</a>, <a href="https://www.gtcountysc.gov/Faq.aspx?QID=116" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgetown FAQ</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/murrells-inlet" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AirROI</a>, <a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr/smallarea/index.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/coderegs/Chapter%2030.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Regs. 30-12</a>, <a href="https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/stationhome.html?id=8661529" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA</a>, <a href="https://www.dnr.sc.gov/marine/shellfish/regs.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDNR</a>, <a href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/NRHP/GetAsset/NRHP/80003670_text" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Register</a>, <a href="https://www.scencyclopedia.org/sce/entries/murrells-inlet/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Encyclopedia</a>. Our counts from both counties' parcels, flood maps and sales. Creek-front: within 30 meters of the salt marsh; the sale count is a floor. Tax: each county's rates and fees for its district. Listings in aggregate from CCMLS. Drives without traffic.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">The Horry side from above: houses on curving streets beside the ponds and fairways of the Indigo Creek golf course. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service.</div><div role="listitem">Wacca Wache Landing on the Waccamaw River, with a marina beside it, on the Georgetown side west of the bypass. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service and added labels placed from map data.</div><div role="listitem">Between the US 17 bypass and Business 17 from above: streets of houses, with a loop street of newer houses in the middle and shops along the bypass at the left. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service and added labels placed from map data.</div><div role="listitem">Houses on the creek side of Business 17 from above, with docks reaching out over the marsh edge to the creek. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service and added labels placed from map data.</div><div role="listitem">The MarshWalk from above: restaurants along the boardwalk at the edge of the inlet, Business 17 behind them, and salt marsh islands in the creek. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service and added labels placed from map data.</div><div role="listitem">Sunnyside in Murrells Inlet: a white one-and-a-half-story cottage with a front gable, a porch on four square columns, two brick chimneys and a red door, with live oaks around a lawn. Photo: Upstateherd, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunnyside_-_Murrells_Inlet_Historic_District.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Resized by Chapter3 Realty.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them. Each photo keeps the license listed with it.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-horry-side-from-above-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-horry-side-from-above-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":900,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"The Horry side from above: houses on curving streets beside the ponds and fairways of the Indigo Creek golf course","caption":"The Horry side from above: houses on curving streets beside the ponds and fairways of the Indigo Creek golf course.","description":"Aerial photo of the Horry side of Murrells Inlet: houses on curving streets and cul-de-sacs beside golf fairways, sand bunkers, ponds and woods, with rows of townhouses at the lower left","creator":{"@type":"Organization","name":"USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP"},"creditText":"USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, public domain, via The National Map (USGS)","copyrightNotice":"Public domain (USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP)","license":"https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/","acquireLicensePage":"https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer","isBasedOn":"https://ima